[{:db/id 17592186166750 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f22c7a35-af74-59c8-b71b-cae8347ea97d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f22c7a35-af74-59c8-b71b-cae8347ea97d" :question/id #uuid "f22c7a35-af74-59c8-b71b-cae8347ea97d" :question/math-academy-id "q-37206" :question/problem "Let $f(x,y,z)=xy+yz+{z}^{2},$ where $x={s}^{2}+{t}^{2},$ $y=\\frac{s}{t}$ and $z=s{t}^{2}.$ Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{3{s}^{2}}{t}+{c}_{1}t+{c}_{2}st+{c}_{3}s{t}^{4},\n$$\n\nfind the value of ${c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "![](images/be/be6afcdd0ad9ae0d7ef377c4918442a64e1186c90c25e27ec6c224d816a602fd.png)\n\nThe chain rule for a multivariable function $f(x,y,z)$ with two independent variables $s$ and $t,$ where $x=x(s,t),y=y(s,t)$ and $z=z(s,t),$ can be expressed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂s}=\\frac{∂f}{∂x}\\cdot \\frac{∂x}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\cdot \\frac{∂y}{∂s}+\\frac{∂f}{∂z}\\cdot \\frac{∂z}{∂s}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives of $f$ with respect to $x,y$ and $z:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=y,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=x+z,\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂z}=y+2z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above results in terms of $s$ and $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{s}{t}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & ={s}^{2}+{t}^{2}+s{t}^{2}, \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{s}{t}+2s{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we take the derivatives of $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ with respect to $s,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂s} & =2s, \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂s} & =\\frac{1}{t}, \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂s} & ={t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting all of our derivatives into the multivariable chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂s} & =(\\frac{s}{t})\\cdot 2s+({s}^{2}+{t}^{2}+s{t}^{2})\\cdot \\frac{1}{t}+(\\frac{s}{t}+2s{t}^{2})\\cdot {t}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{s}^{2}}{t}+\\frac{{s}^{2}}{t}+t+st+st+2s{t}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{s}^{2}}{t}+t+2st+2s{t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${c}_{1}=1,$ ${c}_{2}=2$ and ${c}_{3}=2,$ and therefore\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}+{c}_{3}=1+2+2=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f118ee24-10a3-5bda-8238-4be0365cace0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f118ee24-10a3-5bda-8238-4be0365cace0" :answer-field/id #uuid "f118ee24-10a3-5bda-8238-4be0365cace0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ae277bb1-236f-56f1-8a0c-7fd47295108c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d87585d5-b5cd-5fbc-b58c-a3d2c45f4e66" "answer-3856cad9-d2c1-55a4-adf6-784ae35a6aa1" "answer-5c54b913-d15a-53bc-b2c6-f71477530f9a" "answer-17573a89-2ada-5cfd-8592-1b89b18d61f5" "answer-ae277bb1-236f-56f1-8a0c-7fd47295108c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d87585d5-b5cd-5fbc-b58c-a3d2c45f4e66" :answer/id #uuid "d87585d5-b5cd-5fbc-b58c-a3d2c45f4e66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3856cad9-d2c1-55a4-adf6-784ae35a6aa1" :answer/id #uuid "3856cad9-d2c1-55a4-adf6-784ae35a6aa1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5c54b913-d15a-53bc-b2c6-f71477530f9a" :answer/id #uuid "5c54b913-d15a-53bc-b2c6-f71477530f9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17573a89-2ada-5cfd-8592-1b89b18d61f5" :answer/id #uuid "17573a89-2ada-5cfd-8592-1b89b18d61f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae277bb1-236f-56f1-8a0c-7fd47295108c" :answer/id #uuid "ae277bb1-236f-56f1-8a0c-7fd47295108c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-844676a2-0a90-5f03-a7c1-22515b371e49" :activity/id #uuid "844676a2-0a90-5f03-a7c1-22515b371e49" :activity/title "The Multivariable Chain Rule" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050031 :activity/course 17592186046659 :acti